# Testing

## Framework

- `unittest` only — no pytest
- Run: `python3 run-env.py run.py --test` (preferred when `.venv` exists), or `python3 -m unittest test_run -v` / `python3 run.py --test`

## Fixtures

Use realistic git log strings with the project's custom format:

```
Hash:abc Email:user@example.com Name:User Subj:Subject Body:...
Change-Id: I...
<end-of-commit-message>
```

## What to test

- `parse_log()` — deduplication, Change-Id handling, author grouping
- Config read/write — date advancement, argument merging
- Edge cases: missing Change-Id (warn + hash fallback), duplicate subjects

## Patterns

```python
# ✅ Import from module under test
from run import parse_log, SummaryEntry

# ✅ Assert on domain objects
self.assertEqual(parse_log(log), [SummaryEntry(1, "John Doe", "john@example.com")])

# ✅ Capture expected warnings
with self.assertLogs(level=logging.WARNING):
    parse_log(log_without_change_id)
```

Do not mock `git` subprocess calls when testing pure parsing functions.
